 })
diff --color -ruN -x bin -x obj -x dist -x node_modules -x certs -x '*.log' -x '*.png' mid13/SECURITY.md sol13/SECURITY.md
--- a/SECURITY.md	1970-01-01 01:00:00.000000000 +0100
+++ b/SECURITY.md	2026-09-30 12:13:03.777430780 +0200
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Security policy
+
+SecLab is a learning project that is **intentionally insecure at the starting point** (see `docs/00-overview-and-threat-model.md`). The rules below describe how to handle *real* findings — vulnerabilities in the hardened version, in the tutorial text, or in the tooling — and are also a template for your own projects.
+
+## Supported versions
+
+| Version | Supported |
+|---------|-----------|
+| `main` (hardened, all tutorial steps applied) | yes |
+| Starter (before any step) | no — vulnerable by design |
+
+## Reporting a vulnerability
+
+Please **do not open a public issue**. Report privately to **security@seclab.example** (PGP key on request), or use the repository's private vulnerability reporting feature. Include what you found, how to reproduce it, and the impact you expect.
+
+## What to expect
+
+- We acknowledge your report within **3 business days**.
+- We give a first assessment within **10 business days** and keep you informed until it is fixed.
+- We fix confirmed issues within **90 days** (critical ones sooner) and credit you if you wish.
+- We will not take legal action against good-faith research that respects users' data and stays within this policy.
+
+## Scope
+
+In scope: the API, the web app, the infrastructure files in this repository. Out of scope: denial-of-service by volume, social engineering, third-party services (Keycloak, Azure) themselves.
